{"abstract":[{"text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smaller set is; in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order, [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges do","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not matter; isolated vertices are in it. Deterministic, but which minimum set it is depends","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on the search; for one fixed by a rule, see ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumDominatingSet()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumdominatingset()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumDominatingSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each connected component is solved alone; a vertex adjacent to all the others of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component answers alone. Otherwise branch and reduce: after every choice, an undominated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex with one possible dominator gets it, and a vertex whose undominated closed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbourhood lies in another’s is ruled out (a leaf rule that settles paths and many trees"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"outright). The search branches on the most-coverage dominator of an undominated vertex with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the fewest left and prunes on the budget, on the largest coverages, and on a greedy 2-packing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices with no dominator in common, each needing its own; on trees the largest 2-packing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is γ, Meir and Moon 1975). γ comes from a greedy descent and decisions one smaller, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last set found is the answer. Sparse components keep O(n + m) words of state; dense ones"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(mean degree d with d² above c ⌈c \/ 64⌉) use bitset closed neighbourhoods, under 2m words."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Exponential in the component size in the worst case; the search does not check for task"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancellation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1764","fileName":"ExactCovering.swift"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE20minimumDominatingSetSay6VertexQzGyF","role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"minimumDominatingSet()","modules":[{"name":"Covering","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"